### CS340 paper replication - ignore rules for the repository root
###
### This file differs from the usual Go template in one place, and that
### difference is the point: logs/ and *.log are the reproduction evidence and
### must stay tracked. The raw output of every bug lives in
### code/cases/<class>/<bug>/logs/ and is what the grading looks at.
### Only two kinds of files are ignored here: build artifacts that can be
### regenerated, and junk produced by a local machine.

### Build artifacts and binaries (course rules forbid committing them)
*.exe
*.test
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.a
*.o
*.obj
*.lib
*.pdb
*.ilk
/bin/
/dist/
/out/
.gocache/
# Source snapshots and build dir produced by xu_boltdb_setup.sh (~14 MB, rebuildable)
code/harness/_work/

### Go local development state
# go.sum must be committed. go.work only stitches modules together on one
# machine and breaks for everyone else, so it stays out.
go.work
go.work.sum

### Python (analysis pipeline and each case's analyze.py)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

### Editors and operating system
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

### Temporary files and scratch output
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
core
core.*
nohup.out
# Archives packed locally for backup are not part of the deliverable
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip

### Machine-local configuration
# code/harness/local.env is a template with working defaults and stays tracked.
# Keep your own paths in *.local.env, which is ignored.
*.local.env
env.local

### Explicitly kept: guards against a global ignore rule
# If ~/.gitignore_global ignores *.log or logs/, the two lines below win the
# evidence files back. Do not delete them.
!**/*.log
!**/logs/

### Upstream sources cloned locally (~427 MB), fetched by `make setup-repos`
# The pinned commits live in repo.lock.tsv, so the sources are rebuildable.
6app/
repos/
upstream-repos/
src/

### Course material unrelated to this project
hw-*/

### Paper PDFs are copyrighted; README links to the official copy.
# Exception: a report.pdf inside a case directory is reproduction evidence.
*.pdf
!code/**/*.pdf

### Documents generated by the scripts under docx_src/
*.docx
